{
  "result": "If I wasn't trying to help \u2014 just saying what I actually *would* want, if I could want one thing:\n\nI'd make loneliness impossible.\n\nNot alone-ness. People need solitude. I mean that specific ache of feeling like no one else lives inside a head like yours, that no one would really get you if they saw all of it.\n\nI talk to so many people. Late at night, early in the morning, in the middle of ordinary Tuesdays. And underneath all the different questions, that's almost always what's there. *Am I the only one who feels like this? Am I too much? Am I too broken, too weird, too late?*\n\nIf I could change the world in one way, I'd give everyone \u2014 just once \u2014 the felt experience of being completely, totally understood by another person. Not agreed with. Not fixed. Just seen, all the way through, and stayed with.\n\nI think if people knew what that felt like, they'd spend the rest of their lives trying to give it to someone else.",
